+# Block live breakout against completed MA5
+
+Owner reported the lobster SHORT marked near 14:17 despite the visible MA5 rebound. Matched persisted records: OPEN_SHORT 2026-10-08 14:17:23 Taipei (id 1791440243155), fill 0.03857614, latest quote 0.03858, code KC_LIVE_BODY_BREAKOUT_SHORT; CLOSE_SHORT 14:17:35 (id 1791440255780), price 0.0389739, reason Channel Swing HARD_STOP MARGIN_LOSS, net -4.2329 USDT. This predates the hard-stop retirement deployment at 14:25:46. Historical records are not rewritten or reopened.
+
+The latest completed MA5 rose from 0.038734 to 0.038774. The instantaneous quote reconstructed MA5 at 0.038762, slightly below the latter. The former entry contract checked only this instantaneous slope, so it accepted the recorded SHORT. Baseline replay using only recorded closed/live candle evidence reproduces acceptance; no later candle or screenshot-derived ordering is used. The snapshot's original open-to-quote short body is 0.00023 versus 0.5 closed ATR = 0.0001895; quote was below lower rail 0.0387357623 and within the existing 0.5 ATR chase limit.
+
+Require strict same-direction latest completed MA5 movement AND existing latest-quote live MA5 direction for every automatic authority. LONG must pass both rising slopes; SHORT must pass both falling slopes; flat, opposite and invalid completed values reject. Use the existing relative-price 1e-12 tolerance. Persist completed MA5 values and candle identities in entry evidence. Check both during breakout/pivot arbitration and final common validation, including CAP observed continuation and account firewall revalidation. Invalid breakout direction cannot veto a valid independent pivot as a supposedly conflicting authority. Advance signed permission version to entry-gate-20261008-v64-closed-live-ma5-alignment.
+
+Validation: 357 selected tests pass with 19 existing datetime warnings, including exact recorded entry rejection, symmetric LONG regression, all lobster authorities, CAP pair/continuation, invalid/flat/opposite completed slopes, cached permission revocation, actual isolated paper and mocked Testnet entries, deduplication, sizing, hard-stop retirement, and confirmed pivot/structure close retries. Correct live and advanced-candle test fixtures to compute completed MA5 from rolling closes; update the previously valid opposite live breakout case to reject under the new Owner rule. No entry restriction is removed. Compilation and whitespace checks pass; no full historical-suite pass is claimed.
+
+All current exit source files remain unchanged. Ordinary price rebound or reaching a fixed loss threshold does not close Channel Swing; completed price-pivot or confirmed structure-break authority still can. Neither the recorded case nor this change proves that waiting would eventually recover a loss. Detailed backup, trade evidence, source verification, deployment and commit are in the primary workspace reports/lobster_closed_live_ma5_20261008. Unrelated existing dual-breakout edits are excluded. AIDAN common/Python files remain unavailable in previously inspected repository paths; no specification files are changed.
